<%# src/views/partials/upload-field.ejs
    Shared styled file-upload control: a visually-hidden native input paired
    with a styled label + filename span, so task-photo and avatar uploads
    share one markup structure (issue #79).

    Locals:
      id       (required) - input id; also used as the label's `for`
      name     (required) - input name
      accept   (optional) - input accept attribute
      required (optional) - boolean; adds the required attribute
      multiple (optional) - boolean; adds the multiple attribute (issue #247's
                 memory-batch upload; every other caller omits this and is
                 unaffected)
      label    (optional) - picker button text; defaults to "Choose a photo…".
                 When omitted, this partial's rendered output is byte-for-byte
                 identical to before this local existed (issue #364), so every
                 caller that doesn't pass it is unaffected. The memory batch
                 picker passes "Choose photos…" (issue #364 AC1).

    NOT a local, deliberately: the HTML capture attribute (issue #880). The
    spec frames capture as a hint, but on the affected iOS Safari versions it
    behaves as a directive — it opens the rear camera and drops "Photo
    Library" from the sheet, so a guest cannot reach a photo they already
    took. (Observed first-hand on the owner's iPhone, 2026-07-24; the same
    symptom was recorded as Major-21 in docs/reviews/2026-06-28-adversarial-
    review.md. Behavior has varied across iOS versions, hence "affected".)
    Android likewise skips the app-chooser and goes straight to the camera.

    Omitting the attribute is strictly non-regressive: no browser offers
    FEWER picker options without it than with it, and every OS default picker
    is library-first while still offering the camera. Both deployments render
    this one partial from the single views directory (config.js VIEWS_DIR),
    so the wedding instance and the VARIANT=stag bachelor instance are fixed
    by the same omission.
%>
<div class="upload-field">
  <%# No-JS baseline: this visible text intentionally mirrors PLACEHOLDER /
      uploadLabelText('') in src/public/js/upload-filename.js. AC3 requires
      this label render server-side so the control works with no JS; AC1
      requires the helper return the same copy once JS wires the filename
      display. This is the one remaining, deliberate duplication (for the
      default singular label only — the multiple-picker's plural placeholder
      is read from this label's own text at runtime, see upload-filename.js,
      so it is not duplicated a third time). %>
  <label class="btn" for="<%= id %>"><%= (typeof label !== 'undefined' && label) ? label : 'Choose a photo…' %></label>
  <input type="file"
         id="<%= id %>"
         name="<%= name %>"
         <% if (typeof accept !== 'undefined' && accept) { %>accept="<%= accept %>"<% } %>
         <% if (typeof required !== 'undefined' && required) { %>required<% } %>
         <% if (typeof multiple !== 'undefined' && multiple) { %>multiple<% } %>
         class="visually-hidden" />
  <span class="upload-filename"></span>
</div>
